cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use radarvitals-audit, please cite it as below."
title: "radarvitals-audit: evaluation floors and split files for learned radar vital-sign estimation on the Schellenberger dataset"
abstract: >-
  On the public clinical radar dataset of Schellenberger et al. (24 GHz radar, 30 adults, ECG and continuous finger
  pressure), the within-subject evaluation protocols used by learned heart-rate and blood-pressure estimators are
  matched by a lookup of each subject's resting value, and a generic network that reaches the same errors identifies
  the subject from a radar window with 99% accuracy. On held-out subjects the network falls to the population median
  at rest, while the dataset authors' own classical pipeline scores 0.6 beats per minute. Pooling the five recording
  scenarios makes subject-disjoint heart rate learnable. radarvitals-audit holds the window and label derivation,
  every estimator and protocol, the released split files, and tests that pin every number the paper reports.
type: software
